[h1]Mixed Atmospheres: a full gas and liquid simulation overhaul[/h1]

[b]Development proposal and progress update — not yet a playable mod.[/b]
The standalone mixture core and a developer integration probe exist, and the probe has passed inside Windows and Linux ONI. Complete liquid transport and authoritative integration with ONI are still required. The first public release is intended to include both gases and liquids.

[h2]Every fluid tile becomes a mixture[/h2]
Each tile keeps the grams of every constituent, alongside temperature, pressure, and occupied volume. Oxygen, nitrogen, carbon dioxide, and trace gases can occupy the same tile. Liquid mixtures and separate immiscible phases are part of the target.

[h2]Breathable air takes more than oxygen[/h2]
Hard mode requires 15–35% O₂ by volume/moles. Easy mode accepts anything from 15% upward. Both also check oxygen partial pressure, carbon dioxide, and harmful contaminants. Nitrogen provides an inert background gas, with guaranteed starting supplies and accessible ways to obtain more. The limits are configurable gameplay rules.

[h2]Pressure, heat, and buoyancy drive movement[/h2]
Warm or lighter mixtures rise relative to their surroundings; denser mixtures sink. Gases diffuse rather than stacking into perfectly pure layers. Liquids need realistic volume, pressure, mixing, and separation behavior. Phase changes must account for latent heat and vapor partial pressure.

[h2]Machines must account for their inputs and outputs[/h2]
Pumps move mixtures. Filters separate constituents. Pipes and tanks retain everything they receive. Fuel generators need oxidizer and produce exhaust. Electrolysis, metabolism, crops, critters, and other material conversions must conserve matter and account for energy. Environmental fires and explosions are outside the scope.

[h2]Tools to make the colony playable[/h2]
Planned additions include mixture and partial-pressure overlays, air-quality sensors, ventilation, accessible CO₂ scrubbing, pressure control, nitrogen reserves, and later air-separation equipment. Starting colonies must have the supplies and research access needed to survive the new rules.

[h2]Compatibility and development status[/h2]
The target is new colonies in the base game and Spaced Out!, on Windows and Linux. Existing saves will not be converted. The inspected ONI build is 744825.

ONI's native simulator handles much more than fluids, so replacing it requires careful work on thermal systems, callbacks, saves, and every fluid-using building. The current reference solver is useful for physics tests but does not yet meet colony-scale performance targets. No release date or Workshop download is available yet.

Private native-engine tests on Windows and Linux have also demonstrated importing a fresh world with its fluids captured separately, while the original engine retains solid heat conduction. This is an integration milestone, not a playable colony or complete fluid replacement.
